# --- OIDC provider (generic, provider-neutral) ---
# When set, these point the login flow at any standard-OIDC provider and take
# precedence over the VITE_DESCOPE_* variables below (which remain as a
# backward-compat fallback). Leave unset to keep using Descope.
#
# Example: Ory Network
# VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://inspiring-nash-yli2uiwmcw.projects.oryapis.com
# VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=58142046-5beb-420e-a4cd-310f7263357f
# VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email offline_access
# VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000
#
# Example: the compose Keycloak (`docker compose --profile keycloak up`).
# The first sign-in asks for `organization` with no alias: Keycloak puts the
# user's only organization in the token, or asks a member of several which.
# Choosing another tenant signs in again with the tenant scope template, whose
# {tenant} is replaced by the organization alias. Keycloak refresh tokens need
# no extra scope.
# VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=http://keycloak.localhost:8180/realms/identity-stack
# VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=member-app
# VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email organization
# VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000
# VITE_OIDC_TENANT_SCOPE_TEMPLATE=openid profile email organization:{tenant}
#
# VITE_OIDC_TENANT_SCOPE_TEMPLATE is the whole scope of a sign-in to one tenant,
# for a provider that keeps the tenant in the token. Leave it unset for a
# provider whose tenant is chosen in the app (Descope, Ory): the switch then
# stays client-side.

# --- Descope (backward-compat fallback) ---
# Descope Project ID (required unless the VITE_OIDC_* vars above are set)
VITE_DESCOPE_PROJECT_ID=your-descope-project-id

# Descope Base URL (optional, for custom domains; defaults to https://api.descope.com)
# VITE_DESCOPE_BASE_URL=https://auth.yourdomain.com

# Absolute base URL for API calls. Empty (the default) means the
# frontend uses relative `/api/...` URLs and nginx's `/api/` proxy
# forwards them to the backend on the same origin (standalone mode).
# In gateway mode, docker-compose.gateway.yml sets this to
# http://localhost:8080 so the browser hits Tyk directly. Vite inlines
# the value at build time, so each mode needs its own image.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
